A||N||1||rnoswal||How much wiring do I need?||||5||
Z||000000||rnoswal||02-05-2001||11:09 PM||||I am putting a 2.8 in my 4 cyl 85. How much of the wiring do I need for the swap? I know that the stuff on the engine stays and where it plugs into the box over the driver rear wheel seems the same as mine too. do I need from there on too. Or do I just need the ecm and does that plug into the existing plug from my 4 cyl ecm? How about the tach? Will it read the sixes rpm? And, is the voltage to the old 4 cyl pump the same as the voltage to the 6 cyl pump?<P>Thanks<BR>Russ<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-06-2001||01:28 AM||||You will need the entire engine harness and the computer naturally. This includes the portion that goes inside the car and plugs into the computer, attached is also the connections you spoke of at the battery. Also you need to change the fuel pump in order for the engine to have sufficent fuel pressure to run. The tach will need to be modified with a resistor. Do a search in the archives or visit OGRE'S cave (link at bottom of page)for the info!||||reg||1
